{
  "id": "hayachine_kagura",
  "name": "Hayachine kagura (Iwate yamabushi kagura)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Hayachine kagura is the yamabushi kagura of the Take and Ōtsugunai troupes of Ōhasama in Hanamaki, Iwate, performed at the Hayachine shrine festival in August and in village houses through the year; it is inscribed on UNESCO's Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity. Masked dances of gods, warriors and a sacred lion are accompanied by a drum, hand cymbals and a transverse flute, with chanted verses. The membrane-drum card stands in for the kagura drum, the cymbals card for the hand cymbals and the kagurabue card for the flute.",
  "recipe": "classic modern hayachine kagura, ritual Devotional, indigenous branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment, single lead single track no stacking. membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane drum, credited cymbals, kagurabue. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
